# Shell scripts must reach the image with LF endings.
#
# docker-entrypoint.sh runs as the container ENTRYPOINT. A CRLF line ending on
# its shebang makes the kernel look for an interpreter literally named
# "/bin/sh\r", which does not exist -- the container then fails to start at
# all, on every deploy, with an error that names neither line endings nor the
# file. It is stored LF today only because the machine that wrote it happens
# to normalise on commit; this makes it true regardless of anyone's settings.
*.sh text eol=lf
